# Automatic Post-Change Validation

You MUST validate changes **before** reporting done to the user after any of these tasks:

- Refactoring (rename, extract, move, inline, delete) touching 2+ files
- Adding or removing a feature, view, service, or model
- Changing a service API (method signature, return type, parameters)
- Deleting files or folders
- Adding/removing enum cases

Skip validation only for trivial changes (single-line fix, comment edit, token swap).

## How to Run

The project has three custom subagents in `.cursor/agents/` that handle validation automatically:

- **`style-auditor`** — checks AppStyle token usage (readonly, runs on changed .swift files)
- **`docs-sync-agent`** — updates architecture.md when structure changes
- **`post-change-validator`** — checks dead code, missed reuse, referential integrity, **state propagation** (readonly, background)

If the subagents are not triggered automatically, delegate to them explicitly or fall back to the `post-change-validation` skill manually:

1. Identify changed files via `git diff --name-only` or from the edits you just made
2. Follow the full checklist in the `post-change-validation` skill
3. Report findings inline — do NOT ask the user whether to validate, just do it
4. You MUST fix all findings before reporting done (or flag items that need user decision)
5. You MUST also verify that `architecture.md` was updated if the change added/removed features, services, models, navigation destinations, or shared components
6. When refactoring `ObservableObject` ViewModels or Coordinators, also follow the `post-refactoring-checklist` rule for state propagation verification

